    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nTwo files, one new small function class plus one YAML wiring edit \u2014 no growth of any existing method.\n\n**New step \u2014 `ValidateTelephoneLength.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`): a single-method class that reads the already-normalised E.164 telephone and rejects when the national-number count is wrong for the country:\n- `+61` \u2192 must be 9 national digits (total length 12)\n- `+1` \u2192 must be 10 national digits (total length 12)\n- other country codes are left untouched\n\nIt reuses the existing `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (already the project's telephone-\u2192-400 path, so no new exception or escalation handler files).\n\n**Wiring \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`**: inserted `validateTelephoneLength` between `normalize` (which produces the E.164 value) and `normalizeEmail`.\n\n## Why this shape\n\nThe step runs *after* normalization, so it validates the canonical E.164 form (`+61XXXXXXXXX`), not the raw input. It's a cohesive new unit with `WMC_other = 0` and low cyclomatic complexity, so it doesn't add surrounding complexity to any existing class \u2014 the biggest cost lever. The valid seed/test telephones stay valid: `uniqueTelephone()` yields `+61` + 9 national digits, and the `+1` seed data has 10.\n\nNote the given test input `\"+61 123\"` was already rejected by the total-length floor; the real added behaviour is catching numbers that pass the 8\u201315 total-length check but have the wrong *per-country* national length (e.g. `+61` with 8 national digits).\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` passes and `mvn test` reports BUILD SUCCESS (1 test, 0 failures).",
